##
## Make sure we have firmware installed. Recent versions of live-build have
## some built-in logic to automatically install the right firmware, but for
## that we need DEP-11 metadata in the repository, and Kali has no such.
##
## Baseline: curated common firmware only (replaces full kali-linux-firmware
## collection to keep the ISO < 2 GiB). Covers free firmware, common Intel/AMD
## GPU, and common WiFi/Ethernet. Exotic hardware may need extra firmware later.
firmware-linux-free
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
#if ARCHITECTURES amd64 i386
amd64-microcode
intel-microcode
#endif

##
## Make sure we install as many input/video drivers as we can. Note that
## these packages need to be explicitly listed if we want to be sure that
## they're installed. Installing xserver-xorg is not enough to make sure,
## due to its dependencies, defined as such:
##  * xserver-xorg-input-all | xorg-driver-input
##  * xserver-xorg-video-all | xorg-driver-video
##
xserver-xorg-input-all
xserver-xorg-video-all

## Ensure users of the TTY console can change the keyboard layout. Check
## https://bugs.debian.org/1070679 for details
console-data
